give British agents in Abyssinia diplomatic immunity. He says, you know, my word is law and anything that undermines our sovereignty I'm not happy with. So I don't really want to sign a treaty with you actually. And Plowton thinks, well, fine, maybe he'll come around in time. And actually, Teotros doesn't seem like a terrible investment. So Flashman paints him as this, you know, demonic kind of drunken maniac. But there are lots of ways in which he's actually quite forward thinking. He's a would-be moderniser, actually. He wants to stamp out the power of the regional warlords. He wants to build a new road network. He wants a new system of royal justice. You could see him as a sort of Henry the 7th or something, you know, wanting to impose order after years of chaos.
给予英国在阿比西尼亚的代理人外交豁免权。他说，你知道，我的话就是法律，任何削弱我们主权的事情我都不高兴。所以我真的不想和你签条约。普劳登想，好吧，也许他以后会想通的。实际上，提奥多罗斯看起来并不像一个糟糕的投资。所以弗莱什曼把他描绘成一个恶魔般的、醉醺醺的疯子。但在很多方面，他实际上是相当有前瞻性的。他实际上是一个想成为现代化者的人。他想铲除地方军阀的权力。他想建立一个新的道路网络。他想要一个新的皇家司法系统。你可以把他看作是亨利七世之类的人，你知道，想在多年混乱后强加秩序。

