00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:49.000
He wants to fight slavery because, of course, the slave trade across the Red Sea and the Indian Ocean is controlled by his Muslim rivals. And is that a kind of a gesture of economic warfare against the Ottomans or is there any humanitarian impulsar at all? That is a hard thing to say because although we know of we don't really have that much insights into his inner world, I suspect there's an awful lot of kind of political expediency in it, frankly. He also wants very Peter the Great-like. He wants to change the way people dress. So he wants Abyssinians to wear proper clothes. He wants the them to wear shirts with special coloured sleeves if they've done great service to the state.
他想打击奴隶制，因为当然，跨越红海和印度洋的奴隶贸易是由他的穆斯林对手控制的。这是一种针对奥斯曼人的经济战姿态，还是有任何人道主义冲动？这很难说，因为虽然我们知道，我们并没有真正深入了解他的内心世界，但我怀疑其中有大量的政治权宜之计，坦率地说。他还非常像彼得大帝。他想改变人们的着装方式。所以他想让阿比西尼亚人穿得体的衣服。他想让他们穿袖子上有特殊颜色的衬衫，如果他们为国家做出了巨大贡献的话。

