Proudon said he was very hot-tempered and proud. He goes, ballistic at this, he locks up the patriarch for a little while, and the rumours sweep Abyssinia, well, Teodros has fallen under the sway of the English. Maybe he's going to convert to Protestantism. And he doesn't. Eventually he releases this patriarch and he kneels to ask his forgiveness. And he says, I'm sorry, I've locked you up. And Cyril says, the problem of the years you've been listening to English visitors, don't trust the English. They're only pretending to be your friends. They are plotting, and I quote, to undermine your power and conquer your country.
普劳登说他脾气暴躁且骄傲。他疯了，他把牧首关了一段时间，谣言席卷了阿比西尼亚，好吧，提奥多罗斯已经落入了英国人的控制之下。也许他要皈依新教了。但他没有。最终他释放了这位牧首，并跪下请求他的宽恕。他说，对不起，我把你关起来了。西里尔说，这些年来你一直听信英国访客的问题，不要相信英国人。他们只是假装是你的朋友。他们正在密谋，我引用，‘削弱你的权力并征服你的国家’。

