00:20:46.000 --> 00:21:22.000
How are you? Are you well? I am well, thank God. I have received your envoy with love and friendship. Now you are the child of Christ and I am the child of Christ. For the love of Christ, I want friendship. So that's nice. That's a great letter. It's a fantastic letter. How are you? Are you well? I'm well. I love it. I think he's my favourite Abyssinian King. It's basically like a cold call from a call centre, isn't it? How are you? How's your day going? No, it's not. It's like a pen pal. Yes, that's what it's like. So the other letter is from Plowden to the Foreign Office. And Plowden says, I think we should cement the relationship with Ebassinia.
你好吗？你还好吗？我很好，感谢上帝。我怀着爱和友谊收到了你的特使。现在你是基督的孩子，我也是基督的孩子。为了基督的爱，我想要友谊。所以这很好。这是一封很棒的信。你好吗？你还好吗？我很好。我喜欢它。我想他是我最喜欢的阿比西尼亚国王。这基本上就像来自呼叫中心的冷呼叫，不是吗？你好吗？你今天过得怎么样？不，不是。这就像笔友。是的，就是这样。所以另一封信是普劳登写给外交部的。普劳登说，我认为我们应该巩固与阿比西尼亚的关系。

41
00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:51.000
Could you please send Teodros some guns and ammunition and a handsome piece for his own use, like a hunting rifle? This is in 1857 and two years go by and Plowden and Teodros hear nothing back. And then at last, Plowden gets a message from the coast. London of sent him a package. What is it? There's a rifle, a screwdriver and a case. It's unclear whether the case is for the rifle or the screwdriver. It's for the screwdriver.
你们能给提奥多罗斯送些枪支弹药和一件供他个人使用的精美武器吗，比如猎枪？这是在1857年，两年过去了，普劳登和提奥多罗斯什么回音也没收到。然后终于，普劳登从海岸收到了一条消息。伦敦给他寄了一个包裹。是什么？有一把步枪、一把螺丝刀和一个盒子。不清楚盒子是给步枪的还是给螺丝刀的。是给螺丝刀的。

42
00:21:51.000 --> 00:22:08.000
And that is it. And his heart sinks because he knows this won't go down well with your dross. Not even a letter. And the truth is, of course, the foreign office don't really care. Abyssinia is like a massive backwater. No one really cares about it. It's also they've had the Indian mutiny raging, haven't they? So they've had other things on their mind.
就是这样。他的心沉了下去，因为他知道这在提奥多罗斯那里不会有好结果。甚至连一封信都没有。事实当然是，外交部根本不在乎。阿比西尼亚就像一个巨大的死水。没人真正在乎它。而且他们还经历了印度兵变，不是吗？所以他们有其他事情要考虑。

43
00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:30.000
They've got other things on their mind. Anyway, time goes by. Teodros gets on with fighting the kind of regional warlords and trying to unite the kingdom. But it's much bloodier and more grueling than he expected. He stamps out one rebellion, another breaks out in the next door province. And at one point he says to Plowden, I have deceived myself. This is a stiff-necked people.
他们有其他事情要考虑。总之，时间流逝。提奥多罗斯继续与地方军阀作战，试图统一王国。但这比他预期的要血腥和艰苦得多。他平定了一场叛乱，邻近省份又爆发了另一场。有一次他对普劳登说，我欺骗了自己。这是一群顽固的人。

44
00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:54.000
And it is necessary to chastise them before they enjoy the blessings which Providence has intended. He speaks always in this very kind of rolling biblical cadences. And then in 1858, a key moment, I think, his wife, who was always a moderating influence on him, it was called Tewabak. She died in her late 20s, and he was absolutely bereft. He married again for political reasons.
在他们享受天意所预定的祝福之前，有必要惩罚他们。他说话总是带着这种非常滚动的圣经韵律。然后是1858年，一个关键时刻，我想，他一直作为他温和影响力的妻子，叫特瓦巴克（Tewabak），她在20多岁时去世了，他完全悲痛欲绝。他为了政治原因再次结婚。

45
